      "value": "@{687c1606c1f0e1f01658827d|full_name} I think I've seen tupper once say on Twitter somewhere, they don't really care if you post a duplicate because the time spent searching for existing issues could be less than the time spent reporting the bug. Thanks for the bug report.\n\nThe short answer is YouTube stopped supporting an older version of a YouTube app (version 1.65.10) on Android VR (`android_vr`) headsets (e.g. Meta Quest HMDs), which also affected yt-dlp in VRChat (which pretends to be an Android based VR device with YouTube app version 1.65.10 to download videos from YouTube) for everyone on every platform (including Windows).\n\nThe upstream yt-dlp project \"fixed\" this in a new version by changing the default yt-dlp client list to pretend to be an Apple Vision Pro virtual reality goggles device (`visionos`) instead of an Android VR device, and pretend to be an embedded YouTube video player on a webpage  (`web_embedded`) as a fallback if that fails. VRChat can't use the available video/audio formats available from the prior, but it can use legacy formats from the latter.\n\nThe playback fix is to update yt-dlp in VRChat (the above feature request), which will change the default client list from `android_vr` to a fallback to `web_embedded`. (Non-VR `android` client impersonation would also work, but it's not the default at this time.)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
